[node name="Tunnels" type="Node3D" parent="." unique_id=855103381]

[node name="elevator_bay_link" type="Node3D" parent="Tunnels" unique_id=765276768]
script = ExtResource("3_smlkf")
from_space = NodePath("../../Spaces/mine_mouth")
to_space = NodePath("../../Spaces/elevator_winze_base")
width = 2.4
height = 2.4
tags = Array[StringName]([&"winze"])
notes = "A GRAPH EDGE, NOT A PASSAGE. Reachability is over tunnels, so without this the two winze markers are an island and MineLevel.validate reports both as unreachable - which is false, since the bay opens straight into the chamber.

Deliberately narrow. Its centreline runs from the chamber's centre out to the bay's foot and never leaves the chamber, so at 2.4 m its bore is swallowed whole and carves nothing new; _overrun_at then reaches at most 1.2 m past the foot, which stops 0.6 m short of the bay's west wall. Widen it and it punches through the flat wall the hoist frame stands against, which is the one thing the bay exists to provide."

[node name="elevator_winze" type="Node3D" parent="Tunnels" unique_id=765276767]
script = ExtResource("3_smlkf")
from_space = NodePath("../../Spaces/elevator_winze_base")
to_space = NodePath("../../Spaces/elevator_winze_head")
width = 5.7
height = 5.7
tags = Array[StringName]([&"winze"])
notes = "The elevator bay: a rectangular prism cut up through the west wall of mine_mouth, which is a sphere and therefore had no flat wall to stand a hoist frame against.

SQUARE AND NOT ROUND, and that is the tag's doing. \"winze\" is not in LevelGeometryBuilder.round_profile_tags, so _span_brush emits a CSGBox3D rather than a cylinder - flat walls, a flat floor and flat corners, which is the whole point. Add the tag to that list and this becomes a borehole.

5.7 m clears the 4.92 m frame with room for the collar's flange to bury itself 0.27 m into rock on every side, which is what leaves no seam at the ceiling. The bore runs from the pad's underside up past the chamber's roof; everything above the collar is a dark pocket nobody can reach, and is meant to be."

